# A deploy removes the previous build's files under /assets. A request for one that is gone must
# get a 404: the catch-all below would answer it with index.html and a 200, which a module import
# cannot run and a cache can keep under the file's name. Netlify serves a file that exists before
# it applies any rule, so existing assets are untouched. The first matching rule wins, so this line
# stays above the catch-all.
/assets/*    /404.html     404
/*    /index.html   200
